<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index up 4 to 1511.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index up 4 to 1511.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, Jan 13, Reuter - The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,511 today from 1,507 on Jan 10, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route			  Index    Rate    Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1   US GULF/ARA	  1661    15.081    1668    15.144</p>
<p>   1a  TRANSATLANTIC RV   1640 12419.000    1642 12438.000</p>
<p>   2   US GULF/JAPAN	1883    26.906    1865    26.650</p>
<p>   2a  SKAW P/USG/F EAST  1886 15469.000    1894 15531.000</p>
<p>   3   NOPAC/JAPAN	  1604    14.800    1606    14.813</p>
<p>   3a  JAPAN-SK/NOPAC/RV  1443 11388.000    1444 11394.000</p>
<p>   6   HR OR HR-RB/JAPAN  1220    12.588    1213    12.513</p>
<p>   7   HR/ROTTERDAM	 1257     6.119    1234     6.006</p>
<p>   8   QLAND/ROTTERDAM    0919    10.100    0916    10.068</p>
<p>   9   FE/NOPAC/SKAW-P    0923  8069.000    0926  8100.000</p>
<p>  10   TUBARAO/ROTTERDAM  1161     5.863    1142     5.769</p>
